### Pipeline Diagnosis

**Failure layer: writer-model.** Sources are adequate and properly scoped. The assignment is supported. The instructions appear intact. The deterministic gate cleared correctly given what it evaluates. The failure is entirely in the writer-model execution: the final body section was generated with the same two-paragraph block emitted three times, a classic token-repetition artifact. Because the defect is isolated to a bounded section of body copy and requires only deletion (not fabrication of new evidence or structural redesign), this is revision-eligible. No replay of sources or assignment is warranted.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;cO-BEc9VjPJ7OZwcHYz85GsLTxlQir1Z1DcZyZ0veEQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;npLuPeJjyyzE5ZAT99vmBMkDf1Pewjdmp-7tHC7fBMQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyğDUPLICATE BODY CONTENT: Within the 'What the Forum Makes Legible' H2 section, the two-paragraph block beginning 'The struggles of Indigenous Newar communities in Nepalâ€¦' and the following paragraph beginning 'The challenges facing Indigenous peoples vary across regionsâ€¦' appear three times consecutively. Delete the second and third copies, retaining exactly one instance of each paragraph. After deletion, verify the section reads as a single continuous argument without repeated sentences.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2kkQ3BV9x36J7CwpQcGVqhAp98KG0j12uWUNb-alY50ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyFOOTER SOURCE MISMATCH: The manuscript's frontmatter declares referenceCount:2 (matching the two formal references), but the Sources footer lists four entries including [3] 'Meet Our 2026 Cohort of Indigenous Youth Fellows' and [4] 'Bridging Tradition and Technology,' neither of which is cited in the body or supports any claim in the manuscript. Remove [3] and [4] from the footer, or â€” if they are intended to provide broader research context â€” add a brief inline citation in the body that justifies their inclusion.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;dOjOqEy5QLz-GAtoApEmDQTyNjOAoDgaUQWY1srWgc4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyšDEMAND-LENS H2 (warning, non-blocking per gate): The deterministic gate flagged demand-lens-missing-h2 at severity:warning. None of the three H2 headings currently signals the reader-demand or stakes framing the reporting supports. Consider renaming one heading (e.g., 'What the Forum Makes Legible' â†’ 'What Governments Owe and What They Deliver') to naturally carry that signal without forcing keyword copy.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;wmYeLITKzmMcKCN75li2r3CcFKUQg3aXzOOT_EmfXYsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyöThe manuscript is structurally coherent and its material claims are supported by witnessed evidence, but the final body section contains a severe drafting defect: a two-paragraph block about Nepal/Khokana and regional decision-making is copy-pasted verbatim three times in succession. That repetition disqualifies the draft under the non-repetitive prose standard despite the deterministic gate returning publishable:true. The repair is bounded and does not require replaying sources or the assignment.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;pnN7nPA1AtN53Qeq5QTD8I7ODH5Ku-oT_N5ZNiFBrksƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkwsubmit_revision_requestƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;tjNBIDLxKekhdODSLRwP3aXQepHkiG6PI4oEkM-pCVQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkgsuccessƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;5bXCve